# .trivyignore — CVE suppression register for the pinned base images (#1043).
#
# Policy (docs/codebase/security.md, "Trivy CVE policy"):
#   - One entry per CVE, with the date added, a 90-day expiry, and an inline
#     justification. Nothing global, nothing open-ended.
#   - Only CVEs WITHOUT an available fix (trivy "Fixed version" empty) may be
#     listed. A CVE with a Fixed version is NEVER ignored — re-pin the base
#     image to a rebuilt digest instead (fail-closed).
#   - `--ignore-unfixed` is never used on the command line; the per-CVE
#     register above is the only sanctioned suppression mechanism.
#   - Every entry is re-justified at expiry (2026-12-26); stale entries are
#     removed and the gate fails again until the CVE is fixed upstream or the
#     justification is renewed with fresh evidence.
#
# Created: 2026-09-27 against the trivy DB of that date, for the digests
# pinned in Dockerfile (issue #1043):
#   node:24-bookworm-slim@sha256:0e0ff40c39bc087845bfb27465a0df4ea419520094bc35842ff83dd8cbe6f9b6
#   python:3.12.14-slim-bookworm@sha256:392307d22300de8b5986851a12d9176dfc0fc073e65bf6523ebd7dcbeb23564e

# zlib1g 1:1.2.13.dfsg-1 (both images) — minizip weak encryption; Debian 12 has no fixed release (wontfix for 1.2.13).
CVE-2023-45853  # 2026-09-27; expires 2026-12-26; no fix available in bookworm zlib1g; minizip path not exercised by npm ci / uvicorn runtime

# ncurses 6.4-4 (both images) — heap overflow in ncurses; no bookworm security update yet.
CVE-2025-69720  # 2026-09-27; expires 2026-12-26; no fix available in bookworm ncurses (6.4-4); terminal library not attacker-facing in these images

